Σαβῖνον ἔλαιον, oil
from over-ripe olives, opp.ὠμοτριβές, Gal. 11.872 , Aët. 1.99 , Alex.Trall. 1.12 ;
old oil, Paul.Aeg. 7.3 .

σάρκ-ωσις,εως,ἡ,
growth of flesh, Herod.Med. ap. Orib. 10.9.1 , Aret. CD 1.2 : also,=foreg., Dsc. 5.117 , Gal. 10.446 ;
fleshiness, Id. 1.342 .

σεῖσις,εως,ἡ, (σείω)
shaking, Aret. CA 2.2 ;
concussionof the spine, Gal. 18(1).496 , al.

σεμνολογ-ία,ἡ,
boasting, Chrysipp.Stoic. 3.50 ;
impressiveness, D.H. Comp. 11 , Th. 23 , 50 , App. Syr. 10 .

λοχοέω,
secrete saliva, Hp. Vict. 2.47 ;
slaver, Id. Morb. 3.10 .

Σιβυλλ-ιστής,οῦ,ὁ,
believer in the Sibyl, Cels. ap. Origenes Cels. 5.61 ;
seer, diviner, Plu. Mar. 42 .

σῐνᾰμωρ-ία,ἡ,
mischievousness, joined withὕβρις, Arist. EN 1149b33 ;
greediness, Sch. Ar. Av. 1690 ;
extravagance, Them. Or. 23.294a .

σίσυς,ὁ,=σισύρα, Hsch. ;
any coarseor
cheap garment, Tz.ad Lyc. 634 .

σιφαῖος ἄρτος,ὁ , dub. in Luc. Lex. 6 ;
σιλφαῖος
Suid.

σκηνοποι-ία,ἡ,
tent-making: pitching of tents, Aen.Tact. 8.3 , Rev.Arch. 3(1934).40 (Amphipolis,iii/ii B.C.), Plb. 6.28.3 ;
building of a theatre, D.C. 67.2 ;
nest-building, of swallows, Antig. Mir. 37 : metaph.,ς. τῆς τύχης
